{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain","id":985695,"title":"Carthian-Ruled Domain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T14:50:08-07:00","id":985695,"title":"Carthian-Ruled Domain","content":"So I posted about this in a separate thread, but in the chronicle I'm running soon, the Carthians overthrew the Invictus, after the previous prince's excesses and other issues I still need to hash out.<br /> <br /> The Carthians themselves are somewhat numerous in light of their success, and are primarily divided into three factions (and yes, they're all leftist): Anarchists, communists, and social democrats. These three groups are fairly disparate and have plenty of reasons to distrust and dislike each other. A big problem for the communists is that it's 1976 and the cold war is going strong. Another issue for them is the split between &quot;tankies&quot;* and those who are not.<br /> <br /> The anarchists have issues with establishing an authority - even a Carthian authority - vs. other alternatives. This group is the least homogeneous and most argumentative.<br /> <br /> The social democrats somewhat cynically and definitely ruthlessly got the cooperation from the other factions in staging the coup simply because they represented less of a threat than the Invictus (and exaggerated the threat the Invictus represented, although the prince was downright terrible and many would agree he needed to go).<br /> <br /> I plan the chronicle to cover a few decades (hence starting in 1976, 10 years after the coup itself). At first, the Invictus will represent an external threat to the Invictus that guarantees some level of cooperation. As time passes, however, this spirit of cooperation is likely to fade, and the social democrats will throw their rivals to the wolves should matters come to that.<br /> <br /> The Invictus are relatively weak at first, and at least give lip service to the notion of fealty to the Carthian prince. In the Invictus' eyes, the biggest thing the Carthians had going for them was that the Invictus was ready to depose the prince as well - and said prince was responsible for weakening the Invictus in the first place.<br /> <br /> So there's going to be a lot of tension between the Invictus and the Carthians, and among the Carthian factions themselves.<br /> <br /> I'm still debating how I want to do the whole thing, but the overall city government will be the prince, a technically democratically appointed council (not sure how big - I had 10 members before but six or probably eight seems reasonable). The reality is that the Carthians will have the most seats, while other seats are appointed from within the other five covenants (the extra being House Tremere, who threw in with the Carthians when it looked like the Invictus were going to lose and used that to leverage themselves more power in the domain).<br /> <br /> Looking at 1e the positions are:<ul><li>Prince</li> <li>Seneschal</li> <li>Herald</li> <li>Primogen</li> <li>Priscus</li> <li>Whip</li> <li>Harpy</li> <li>Sheriff</li> <li>Hounds</li> <li>Master of Elysium</li> </ul><br /> Not going to fill those roles precisely as described and it looks like a lot of it was dropped in 2e. Just making a note for later.<br /> <br /> * A hardline Stalinist. A tankie is a member of a communist group or a &quot;fellow traveller&quot; (sympathiser) who believes fully in the political system of the Soviet Union and defends/defended the actions of the Soviet Union and other accredited states (China, Serbia, etc.) to the hilt, even in cases where other communists criticise their policies or actions. For instance, such a person favours overseas interventions by Soviet-style states, defends these regimes when they engage in human rights violations, and wishes to establish a similar system in other countries such as Britain and America. (courtesy of Urban Dictionary)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:09:07-07:00","id":985706,"title":"","content":"Something to think about<b></b>: what is the Carthian council responsible for? Distribution of limited resources? What do they have authority over? Havens, feeding rights? Do they seek to influence mortal politics as well, or is this a &quot;socialism in one domain&quot; situation?<br /> <br /> There's a couple of potential breaking points here depending on how much you want to draw on real-world leftist politics. As you say, one threat would be the social democrat faction throwing their rivals to the wolves- EG, European social democrat parties endorsing WW1. An alternative risk could be the communist faction tacitly supporting an Invictus takeover (or some really wild outsider faction like the Crone or the Tremere) to punish the social democrat faction, hoping that the purge of their rivals and the renewed tyranny would inspire a true revolution where the hardliners can take power. And/or, either faction could turn on the anarchist faction and expend their resources trying to control their nominal allies.<br /> <br /> What does anarchy look like in a vampire domain? Is there just no Prince or ruling council, and organization starts with voluntary coteries and grows upward? Do they care about the Masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:20:28-07:00","id":985715,"title":"","content":"I'm still working on what the anarchists' ideal domain would look like, but it'll be very far from the reality.<br /> <br /> The Council is basically the primogen council. They serve as advisors to the prince, have their own power bases, are all elders or ancillae themselves. In theory, the council members are appointed from within the ranks of whichever covenant they're from. In practice, the council has considerable say over who gets to stay on the council. In practice, the most powerful and influential kindred end up there. They have a lot of say in policy, who gets assigned subdomains, etc. but the prince is the final word.<br /> <br /> Many kindred have influence over mortal agencies - whether political, corporate, etc. This isn't something that's necessarily specific to anyone with a title, although those with titles can use their status and personal power to encourage others to use resources on their behalf.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum had some losses of their own when the Invictus was deposed. They're definitely not happy about that, esp. with the Circle's fortunes improving at the Lance's expense (or at least that's how they view it).<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul is mostly investigating splinters, and aren't heavily invested in the local politics. Basically as long as they're left alone to do their thing (and no one really knows what their thing is right now) they'll be happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:24:00-07:00","id":985717,"title":"","content":"I think the one threat of revolution is filling that vacuum. Everyone has different perceptions of what the ideal government is and how they fit within it. If you look at revolutions, the aftermath usually follows one of two models. Either a strongman seizes charge and establishes himself as a dictator by using the necessity of martial law a pretext, or factionalism creates a violent and rapidly shifting political structure in which no one individual or party manages to stay in power for very long.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Carthians, at least early on, will have to maintain some sense of solidarity, since the other covenants are real and present threats, but I wouldn't be surprised if political positions change hands quick and often over the next few decades. I'd imagine it's only after the revolution that things really start to get ruthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:27:17-07:00","id":985719,"title":"","content":"Indeed, that is the plan. The starting point is ten years after the revolution and things have somewhat settled down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:30:08-07:00","id":985721,"title":"","content":"I would note that the listed positions and titles are very much an Invictus structure. I know the 1e core listed them as the default and suggested alternate titles that the other Covenants might use basically the same positions, but Requiem has gradually moved away from such a standardized structure, to the point where 2e didn't even list those titles.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say you shouldn't roll with them. It could be that the social democrat Carthians adopted the existing political structure, perhaps as a way to make the transition less jarring for the citizens, or to assuage the Invictus who might otherwise have opposed them more vehemently. But it's undoubtedly going to be a point of internal contention. I'm sure many Carthians, especially the anarchist faction, would likely see a structure that mirrors Invictus roles as more of the same with different assholes in charge.<br /> <br /> In fact, this is something I have seen come up in and out of character in Requiem LARP all the time. A city is predominantly Carthian, but uses the &quot;traditional&quot; structure, maybe with some small tweaks to who is responsible for what and some titles swapped out, and everyone whispers about how they're not <i>real</i> Carthians, they're just Invictus Lite. In character this usually takes the form of plots to overthrow the current prince or prime minister or president or whatever they call him, more often than not by other Carthians. Out of character it takes the form of people gossiping about how so-and-so doesn't know how to play a Carthian, and how they probably just wanted to play an Invictus but have access to Carthian Law and their proprietary Devotions, or debating about what a well-roleplayed Carthian domain should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:35:00-07:00","id":985724,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wasn't really thinking of using the positions as named and defined, but they serve as a starting point to work out what kind of power structure might work. It's easier for me if I have an outline to start with than if I start from nothing.<br /> <br /> There is definitely an element of appeasing the Invictus going on, and this is a point of contention with the other Carthian factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:38:29-07:00","id":985728,"title":"","content":"Like the only positions I know for sure right now are the Prince (whatever I end up calling him) and the council (effectively the primogen council).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:40:37-07:00","id":985731,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I figured you weren't planning to directly copy that structure. Just offering food for thought based on my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:43:22-07:00","id":985732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985724#post985724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I wasn't really thinking of using the positions as named and defined, but they serve as a starting point to work out what kind of power structure might work. It's easier for me if I have an outline to start with than if I start from nothing.<br /> <br /> There is definitely an element of appeasing the Invictus going on, and this is a point of contention with the other Carthian factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably start with my Prince and use that as the basis for what sort of political structure suits the city. I know that the setting book, <i>Damnation City</i> has some examples of divergent structures. I don't remember how they modeled the Carthian-run city, but there might be interesting stuff in there.<br /> <br /> I've been building out a model for an Atlanta game, and I think something similar could actually make sense for an American city run by a Prince enamored with Soviet politics. Go with a Bureau system, with chiefs and sub-chiefs managing the various aspects of kindred life and overseeing mortal interests. These are, of course, appointed positions, perhaps assigned by a small board of &quot;democratically elected&quot; faction leaders. Of course, the Carthians have managed to get themselves a majority in this Central Committee (but if everyone aligns against the Carthians and they can turn someone, the other powers could turn the sham democracy of the Carthian institution on its head).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:44:31-07:00","id":985733,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> And I appreciate it!<br /> <br /> So like I don't think there will be a herald equivalent at all. I think there will likely be harpies but they won't be a formal position, just, like...they pick themselves, you know? There probably will be something like the sheriff and the hounds but probably with a different name. I am not sure I want clans to be cohesive enough to have whips and prisci. I think there will probably be a seneschal and master of elysium, whatever they're called. Deputy Mayor and Manager of Public Works? IDK. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think that there's definitely enough parallels with Invictus power structures that a lot of this is done to appease other kindred with some level of familiarity, but I see the system growing away from that over time... which will cause some upheaval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:47:43-07:00","id":985736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985732#post985732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd probably start with my Prince and use that as the basis for what sort of political structure suits the city. I know that the setting book, <i>Damnation City</i> has some examples of divergent structures. I don't remember how they modeled the Carthian-run city, but there might be interesting stuff in there.<br /> <br /> I've been building out a model for an Atlanta game, and I think something similar could actually make sense for an American city run by a Prince enamored with Soviet politics. Go with a Bureau system, with chiefs and sub-chiefs managing the various aspects of kindred life and overseeing mortal interests. These are, of course, appointed positions, perhaps assigned by a small board of &quot;democratically elected&quot; faction leaders. Of course, the Carthians have managed to get themselves a majority in this Central Committee (but if everyone aligns against the Carthians and they can turn someone, the other powers could turn the sham democracy of the Carthian institution on its head).</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely gives me something to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:06:14-07:00","id":985747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985736#post985736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That definitely gives me something to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Off the top of my head, I'd probably put together something like this.<br /> <br /> You have a Prince who's the nominal representative of the Carthian Movement. He could be either a paper tiger assigned to placate the feuding Carthian factions or a strong man who uses intimidation and purges to maintain his power.<br /> <br /> A central committee of eight members is in charge of assigning ministers. You have the Prince, a representative from each of the Carthian factions, and one from each of the other covenants. Probably one or two of those leaders are toadies for the Carthians. Nominally, these are democratically elected positions, but it's likely each covenant has their own standards for what &quot;democratic&quot; means.<br /> <br /> As for ministers, I'd imagine secretary of the interior would be the coveted position. She's more or less the Sheriff of the city, but she holds a lot of power. Bureau chiefs beneath her are in charge of dealing with inter-covenant and inter-vampire struggles, keeping an eye on threats from hunters and other supernaturals, and maintaining a ruthless secret police force in place. You probably have a labor minister in charge of a vast department that maintains pawns in the various mortal unions and city hall and a cultural minister promoting the mortal arts and governing the rules and status of elysium. Transportation minister would closely screen who enters and leaves the cities and keeps the public transit system free from internecine squabbles and safe for kindred to travel on.<br /> <br /> Given the cronyism at play in Soviet-era politics and the small population of kindred in any particular city, I'd assume that anyone without some sort of position in one of the bureaus is being singled out as a pariah. I could see a bunch of departments being created for the express purpose of placating other vampires. Maybe the Ordo Dracul has been calmed by being given control of a ministry of research, more or less offered their own expansive domain where they can do whatever they want as long as they support Carthian rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:18:45-07:00","id":985757,"title":"","content":"That's, of course, assuming that it's some coalition of socialist democrats and communists in charge. If the anarchists are in charge, it's bound to be a whole new ball game. I imagine those two groups really have less in common than the non-anarchist Carthians do with the Invictus. I could actually see the Carthian base as a very structured system. Every kindred has their place in the society, and childer rights are carefully doled out (typically through nepotism). They might even win over the Ordo Dracul and the Sanctum to their side, and the anarchists might end up working with the Circle of the Crone to seed another rebellion. I'd think there'd be a lot of crossover between those groups anyway, to a degree where there's a blur between who's a radical member of the Carthians and who's a Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:25:35-07:00","id":985802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985747#post985747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, I'd probably put together something like this.<br /> <br /> You have a Prince who's the nominal representative of the Carthian Movement. He could be either a paper tiger assigned to placate the feuding Carthian factions or a strong man who uses intimidation and purges to maintain his power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to avoid purges under the new regime as one of the reasons the old regime fell was in fact due to purges. Which isn't to say the Carthians would never purge, I just want to avoid that before the chronicle starts. That might mean moving up the date of the revolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985747#post985747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A central committee of eight members is in charge of assigning ministers. You have the Prince, a representative from each of the Carthian factions, and one from each of the other covenants. Probably one or two of those leaders are toadies for the Carthians. Nominally, these are democratically elected positions, but it's likely each covenant has their own standards for what &quot;democratic&quot; means.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works, although I'm more inclined to have eight members + the prince so the prince gets to act as tie breaker as well as place himself above the council. Totally down with everyone getting a seat, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985747#post985747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for ministers, I'd imagine secretary of the interior would be the coveted position. She's more or less the Sheriff of the city, but she holds a lot of power. Bureau chiefs beneath her are in charge of dealing with inter-covenant and inter-vampire struggles, keeping an eye on threats from hunters and other supernaturals, and maintaining a ruthless secret police force in place. You probably have a labor minister in charge of a vast department that maintains pawns in the various mortal unions and city hall and a cultural minister promoting the mortal arts and governing the rules and status of elysium. Transportation minister would closely screen who enters and leaves the cities and keeps the public transit system free from internecine squabbles and safe for kindred to travel on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very nice euphemistic name for the office (Ministry of the Interior). I like this idea for dividing up offices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985747#post985747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the cronyism at play in Soviet-era politics and the small population of kindred in any particular city, I'd assume that anyone without some sort of position in one of the bureaus is being singled out as a pariah. I could see a bunch of departments being created for the express purpose of placating other vampires. Maybe the Ordo Dracul has been calmed by being given control of a ministry of research, more or less offered their own expansive domain where they can do whatever they want as long as they support Carthian rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing is that the socdems are in power whereas the communists are not. The tankies probably are in favor and supporting the prince, or at least wherever the real power is. It may be that the communists are more a part of the power structure simply because the socdems can't fill every role.<br /> <br /> I like that idea for the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985757#post985757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's, of course, assuming that it's some coalition of socialist democrats and communists in charge. If the anarchists are in charge, it's bound to be a whole new ball game. I imagine those two groups really have less in common than the non-anarchist Carthians do with the Invictus. I could actually see the Carthian base as a very structured system. Every kindred has their place in the society, and childer rights are carefully doled out (typically through nepotism). They might even win over the Ordo Dracul and the Sanctum to their side, and the anarchists might end up working with the Circle of the Crone to seed another rebellion. I'd think there'd be a lot of crossover between those groups anyway, to a degree where there's a blur between who's a radical member of the Carthians and who's a Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchists won't be in charge, although they will be recipients of several placatory gestures. A friend suggested something about the anarchists having a lot of crossover with the Circle of the Crone, which sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-11-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:56:29-07:00","id":985822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985802#post985802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am trying to avoid purges under the new regime as one of the reasons the old regime fell was in fact due to purges. Which isn't to say the Carthians would never purge, I just want to avoid that before the chronicle starts. That might mean moving up the date of the revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense. With that kind of history, and with the number of conflicting interests at play, open purges would basically be a death note for the Prince, and it would encourage more clever power plays and coalition building.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985802#post985802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This works, although I'm more inclined to have eight members + the prince so the prince gets to act as tie breaker as well as place himself above the council. Totally down with everyone getting a seat, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also makes sense. Maybe the eighth member is elected via an open election in which all the kindred are allowed to vote?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985802#post985802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a very nice euphemistic name for the office (Ministry of the Interior). I like this idea for dividing up offices.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I'm pulling a lot of ideas from my Atlanta game. It's an Invictus-led city, but Atlanta has something of a weird geography, so I decided to create a political structure that's organic to that. Our city is really, really spread out, so micromanaging physical territories would be very difficult. So what the Invictus Prince has done is turn the Midtown-Downtown corridor into Invictus territory. That's the heart of tourism, traffic, city governance, and upscale real estate. She keeps a lid on power by changing the game and making it about domains of influence rather than domains of territory. Perhaps things are similar in your city, with each covenant essentially having their own physical territories, but control over the city's political and infrastructural levels relegated to bureaucratic positions that's largely dictated by the Carthian elite?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering how exactly the Communist/SocDem split functions. Perhaps the Social Democrats have the strongest power base among kindred, but the Commies have too much mortal influence to ignore? The hardliners have their claws dug deep into the unions and various levels of government, so spurning them would throw the city into disarray and set the stage for a long, protracted war. Conversely, you can't really kick the SDs out because, while their political structure isn't what was once, it's close enough to placate the other covenants. I could actually see a lot of the younger Invictus adapting very well to the new order, ingratiating themselves into the new system. It's still a structure built on cronyism and nepotism, but unlike the entrenched systems of the old Invictus, they actually have a lot more leverage to climb the ladder. I could see a state of affairs where the Invictus is crippled by defections, and the SD arm of the Carthians has become so top heavy as to drown out most of the more radical voices. New boss, same as the old boss kind of thing.<br /> <br /> The anarchists are maybe sprawled out throughout the projects and slowly gentrifying BoHo neighborhoods of the city. They're less a faction than a loosely aligned group of coteries. They present themselves as communal anarchists, but in reality, there's a lot of tensions and turf wars between the different broods. So far, the rulers have more or less left them to their own devices, but tensions are building up. They aren't happy with the new order, and there's a really thin line between them and the Circle, who chafe at the &quot;civilized&quot; pretenses of the New Carthian Order. The Circle and the anarchists are so closely aligned that it can be hard to distinguish who is who, and there are rumors that they're courting the communist hardliners to stage another insurrection. Regardless, they aren't happy. They see this new structure as more or less a second coming of the Invictus, and they aren't too far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T04:46:49-07:00","id":986048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes a lot of sense. With that kind of history, and with the number of conflicting interests at play, open purges would basically be a death note for the Prince, and it would encourage more clever power plays and coalition building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much. If you have Splintered Seattle, the description for Seattle is what led to the current situation. I just moved everything back in time about 50 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also makes sense. Maybe the eighth member is elected via an open election in which all the kindred are allowed to vote?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of having an open election but wasn't sure how to fit it into the way the city was shaping up. This sounds like a great idea, and would motivate the covenants to get their members to act and vote to get extra influence on the council.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks I'm pulling a lot of ideas from my Atlanta game. It's an Invictus-led city, but Atlanta has something of a weird geography, so I decided to create a political structure that's organic to that. Our city is really, really spread out, so micromanaging physical territories would be very difficult. So what the Invictus Prince has done is turn the Midtown-Downtown corridor into Invictus territory. That's the heart of tourism, traffic, city governance, and upscale real estate. She keeps a lid on power by changing the game and making it about domains of influence rather than domains of territory. Perhaps things are similar in your city, with each covenant essentially having their own physical territories, but control over the city's political and infrastructural levels relegated to bureaucratic positions that's largely dictated by the Carthian elite?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea, esp. in context with later comments (such as the communists having a lot of influence with labor). I like the sound of it! Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering how exactly the Communist/SocDem split functions. Perhaps the Social Democrats have the strongest power base among kindred, but the Commies have too much mortal influence to ignore? The hardliners have their claws dug deep into the unions and various levels of government, so spurning them would throw the city into disarray and set the stage for a long, protracted war. Conversely, you can't really kick the SDs out because, while their political structure isn't what was once, it's close enough to placate the other covenants. I could actually see a lot of the younger Invictus adapting very well to the new order, ingratiating themselves into the new system. It's still a structure built on cronyism and nepotism, but unlike the entrenched systems of the old Invictus, they actually have a lot more leverage to climb the ladder. I could see a state of affairs where the Invictus is crippled by defections, and the SD arm of the Carthians has become so top heavy as to drown out most of the more radical voices. New boss, same as the old boss kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too is really cool, and I will certainly work it into things. I especially like the communists having a lot of influence with the unions - something I should have thought of, but didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The anarchists are maybe sprawled out throughout the projects and slowly gentrifying BoHo neighborhoods of the city. They're less a faction than a loosely aligned group of coteries. They present themselves as communal anarchists, but in reality, there's a lot of tensions and turf wars between the different broods. So far, the rulers have more or less left them to their own devices, but tensions are building up. They aren't happy with the new order, and there's a really thin line between them and the Circle, who chafe at the &quot;civilized&quot; pretenses of the New Carthian Order. The Circle and the anarchists are so closely aligned that it can be hard to distinguish who is who, and there are rumors that they're courting the communist hardliners to stage another insurrection. Regardless, they aren't happy. They see this new structure as more or less a second coming of the Invictus, and they aren't too far off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is pretty close to what I had in mind, but better. I mean there is some level of appeasement to the anarchists but it's not really possible to make them <i>happy</i> under the current regime. They fought as hard as anyone to bring down the Invictus prince and are now basically left out in the cold while the communists and socdems (esp. the socdems) divide up all the power and leave them with scraps. Even if that's not 100% true it certainly feels true to them and will become moreso over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:07:43-07:00","id":986140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986048#post986048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, pretty much. If you have Splintered Seattle, the description for Seattle is what led to the current situation. I just moved everything back in time about 50 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking of having an open election but wasn't sure how to fit it into the way the city was shaping up. This sounds like a great idea, and would motivate the covenants to get their members to act and vote to get extra influence on the council.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is an interesting idea, esp. in context with later comments (such as the communists having a lot of influence with labor). I like the sound of it! Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This too is really cool, and I will certainly work it into things. I especially like the communists having a lot of influence with the unions - something I should have thought of, but didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, this is pretty close to what I had in mind, but better. I mean there is some level of appeasement to the anarchists but it's not really possible to make them <i>happy</i> under the current regime. They fought as hard as anyone to bring down the Invictus prince and are now basically left out in the cold while the communists and socdems (esp. the socdems) divide up all the power and leave them with scraps. Even if that's not 100% true it certainly feels true to them and will become moreso over time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Happy to help. I love city building. I'm in the process of putting together setting bibles for 80s Miami (for my present Hunter game) and modern Atlanta (for a future Vampire game). I don't have Splintered Seattle, but it seems like a really cool place to set a game.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, my knowledge of historic Seattle isn't that strong, but there are three historical things that stick in my mind.<br /> <br /> I know they hosted the World's Fair in the early 60s, as an attempt at city revitalization. That could be a cool set piece for the original revolution a decade prior to your game.<br /> <br /> I also know it's always been a pretty big hub for the various (mostly white) counterculture movements. I'm pretty sure your era is about the time the environmentalist movement is taking off. It's highly possible that the Circle is entrenched in some of the more radical elements of that movement, and perhaps that's where they have the strongest crossover with the anarchists.<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't this be around the time Microsoft is starting to develop? Late 70s/early 80s you'll be having the big tech boom and all the money and complications that brings. That transitional period from the 70s to 80s is really interesting to me, and Seattle strikes me as one of those cities where the transition is very apparent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:04:15-07:00","id":986197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986048#post986048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, pretty much. If you have Splintered Seattle, the description for Seattle is what led to the current situation. I just moved everything back in time about 50 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking of having an open election but wasn't sure how to fit it into the way the city was shaping up. This sounds like a great idea, and would motivate the covenants to get their members to act and vote to get extra influence on the council.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is an interesting idea, esp. in context with later comments (such as the communists having a lot of influence with labor). I like the sound of it! Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This too is really cool, and I will certainly work it into things. I especially like the communists having a lot of influence with the unions - something I should have thought of, but didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, this is pretty close to what I had in mind, but better. I mean there is some level of appeasement to the anarchists but it's not really possible to make them <i>happy</i> under the current regime. They fought as hard as anyone to bring down the Invictus prince and are now basically left out in the cold while the communists and socdems (esp. the socdems) divide up all the power and leave them with scraps. Even if that's not 100% true it certainly feels true to them and will become moreso over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would anarchists want involvement in any government structure? The very definition of anarchy is the absence of all forms of government, systems of hierarchy, or that anyone has an inherent right to assert non consentual control over the lives of other individuals. If they don't believe that, or think it only applies situationally or only to certain groups, then they aren't anarchists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:14:33-07:00","id":986203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986197#post986197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would anarchists want involvement in any government structure? The very definition of anarchy is the absence of all forms of government, systems of hierarchy, or that anyone has an inherent right to assert non consentual control over the lives of other individuals. If they don't believe that, or think it only applies situationally or only to certain groups, then they aren't anarchists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them might be pragmatic to recognize that city-wide anarchy is a pipe dream, but that having someone to represent their interests in the existing ideology gives them the leverage to maintain their own territory without intrusion. They could also recognize that anarchy isn't going to happen right away, and by influencing and pushing the political structure further towards an anarchist system suits their best interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-12-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:41:28-07:00","id":986260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986197#post986197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would anarchists want involvement in any government structure? The very definition of anarchy is the absence of all forms of government, systems of hierarchy, or that anyone has an inherent right to assert non consentual control over the lives of other individuals. If they don't believe that, or think it only applies situationally or only to certain groups, then they aren't anarchists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their end goal requires they have some influence over the state as it exists. They don't have to necessarily work within the system (and many don't want to) but being effectively excluded from the system after helping to put an end to the previous system kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> Anarchy is also not a singular thing but several different schools of thought, with different goals and priorities. At least a handful propose variations on democracy and collectivism, which are not entirely inconsistent with helping establish a new Carthian regime. The problem is that they were being used by the SocDems and when the revolution was over had little to no influence on how things turned out. The anarchists would have loved to have had more input with the outcome being a more anarchist society without need for authoritarian centralization of power (and they would argue that such is <i>never</i> needed).<br /> <br /> Does that clarify things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:47:40-07:00","id":986263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986140#post986140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy to help. I love city building. I'm in the process of putting together setting bibles for 80s Miami (for my present Hunter game) and modern Atlanta (for a future Vampire game). I don't have Splintered Seattle, but it seems like a really cool place to set a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Demon supplement so most of it I'm like ??? about what's going on. However, there's a section that describes the state of the city for each of the other game lines, or several of them at least. The Vampire background is that the prince is growing increasingly paranoid and purging anyone he deems disloyal, and everyone else is trying to figure out what to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986140#post986140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, my knowledge of historic Seattle isn't that strong, but there are three historical things that stick in my mind.<br /> <br /> I know they hosted the World's Fair in the early 60s, as an attempt at city revitalization. That could be a cool set piece for the original revolution a decade prior to your game.<br /> <br /> I also know it's always been a pretty big hub for the various (mostly white) counterculture movements. I'm pretty sure your era is about the time the environmentalist movement is taking off. It's highly possible that the Circle is entrenched in some of the more radical elements of that movement, and perhaps that's where they have the strongest crossover with the anarchists.<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't this be around the time Microsoft is starting to develop? Late 70s/early 80s you'll be having the big tech boom and all the money and complications that brings. That transitional period from the 70s to 80s is really interesting to me, and Seattle strikes me as one of those cities where the transition is very apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to the World's Fair: The Century 21 Exhibition in 1962.<br /> <br /> And yes to the mostly white counterculture movements. Environmentalism was a thing for decades before the 70s, but it really came into its own in the 70s thanks to the active counterculture. And I totally agree that the Circle and anarchists are involved.<br /> <br /> Microsoft was founded on April 4, 1975, so good catch on that. For some reason I was thinking they were founded in the 80s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:47:54-07:00","id":986264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986260#post986260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their end goal requires they have some influence over the state as it exists. They don't have to necessarily work within the system (and many don't want to) but being effectively excluded from the system after helping to put an end to the previous system kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> Anarchy is also not a singular thing but several different schools of thought, with different goals and priorities. At least a handful propose variations on democracy and collectivism, which are not entirely inconsistent with helping establish a new Carthian regime. The problem is that they were being used by the SocDems and when the revolution was over had little to no influence on how things turned out. The anarchists would have loved to have had more input with the outcome being a more anarchist society without need for authoritarian centralization of power (and they would argue that such is <i>never</i> needed).<br /> <br /> Does that clarify things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point: libertarian socialism. Which despite sounding like an oxymoron is in fact a political philosophy that could be described as anarchistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:51:59-07:00","id":986273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986263#post986263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Demon supplement so most of it I'm like ??? about what's going on. However, there's a section that describes the state of the city for each of the other game lines, or several of them at least. The Vampire background is that the prince is growing increasingly paranoid and purging anyone he deems disloyal, and everyone else is trying to figure out what to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes to the World's Fair: The Century 21 Exhibition in 1962.<br /> <br /> And yes to the mostly white counterculture movements. Environmentalism was a thing for decades before the 70s, but it really came into its own in the 70s thanks to the active counterculture. And I totally agree that the Circle and anarchists are involved.<br /> <br /> Microsoft was founded on April 4, 1975, so good catch on that. For some reason I was thinking they were founded in the 80s.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually might pick that up (or borrow a copy from my friend who probably has it, as he seems to have EVERY damn ChroD book). I love Demon in theory, but I'd love to see how it works in action.<br /> <br /> MS was founded in 1975, but I don't think they moved their HQ to Redmond until somewhere between 78-80. It should give you a really nice monkey wrench to throw in the works once you've established the state of affairs your characters are operating in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:50:47-07:00","id":986404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986273#post986273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually might pick that up (or borrow a copy from my friend who probably has it, as he seems to have EVERY damn ChroD book). I love Demon in theory, but I'd love to see how it works in action.<br /> <br /> MS was founded in 1975, but I don't think they moved their HQ to Redmond until somewhere between 78-80. It should give you a really nice monkey wrench to throw in the works once you've established the state of affairs your characters are operating in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wiki says they moved to Bellingham in 79 but I didn't read on to see when they moved to Redmond. Microsoft's definitely going to be an important thing in the chronicle. Important to the domain as well as the city.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:55:01-07:00","id":986407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986264#post986264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Case in point: libertarian socialism. Which despite sounding like an oxymoron is in fact a political philosophy that could be described as anarchistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, libertarian seems to mean something different outside the US. <a href=\"http://flag.blackened.net/liberty/moorcock.html\" target=\"_blank\">Someone linked an article by Michael Moorcock the other day</a>, which referred to anarchist politics as libertarian at several points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:00:55-07:00","id":986412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986404#post986404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wiki says they moved to Bellingham in 79 but I didn't read on to see when they moved to Redmond. Microsoft's definitely going to be an important thing in the chronicle. Important to the domain as well as the city.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oops. I was wrong. 1986. But if it's a chronicle spread over multiple decades, that rise to prominence can be a slow boil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:09:08-07:00","id":986420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986412#post986412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oops. I was wrong. 1986. But if it's a chronicle spread over multiple decades, that rise to prominence can be a slow boil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:37:31-07:00","id":986439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=985822#post985822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also makes sense. Maybe the eighth member is elected via an open election in which all the kindred are allowed to vote?</div> </div> </div> </div>The old standard primogen councils give representatives for each covenant. But why not take the open approach for all of the seats with proportional representation? Yes, Carthians could guarantee themselves control by setting them in their favour, but an appeal to fairness that theoretically allows non Carthians a chance to gain the majority could be a winning compromise. The communists probably won't a stand a chance.outside a coalition and the anarchists are sharing the &quot;anti-establishment&quot; vote with the neo-Invictus/Lancea et Sanctum, but it's not constitutionally impossible for the winners of a revolution a lifetime ago to lose the majority at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:08:35-07:00","id":986795,"title":"","content":"Another thing to keep in mind is characters (PCs and NPCs) can belong in more than one covenants. I think that the carthians will be more prone to have members in the other covenant trying to reform them from within. Also the carthians in the other covenant will be factions of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:32:16-07:00","id":989575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=986404#post986404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wiki says they moved to Bellingham in 79 but I didn't read on to see when they moved to Redmond. Microsoft's definitely going to be an important thing in the chronicle. Important to the domain as well as the city.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's Bellevue, not Bellingham. Bellevue is the bigger city right next to Redmond. Bellingahm is a few hours north, almost Canada.<br /> <br /> FYI, I am a Seattle area local (I work in Redmond, not at Microsoft but nearby) and know demon really well. Feel free to tag me if you have questions about the area or Demon's Seattle setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:37:57-07:00","id":989577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=989575#post989575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's Bellevue, not Bellingham. Bellevue is the bigger city right next to Redmond. Bellingahm is a few hours north, almost Canada.<br /> <br /> FYI, I am a Seattle area local (I work in Redmond, not at Microsoft but nearby) and know demon really well. Feel free to tag me if you have questions about the area or Demon's Seattle setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes my brain swaps similar words on me. Something like paraphasia, but not severe.<br /> <br /> And thanks, I may very well have questions for you in the near future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:44:34-07:00","id":989579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=989577#post989577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes my brain swaps similar words on me. Something like paraphasia, but not severe.<br /> <br /> And thanks, I may very well have questions for you in the near future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, no problem. Just pointing out that Microsoft was actually closer to Seattle proper between 79 and 86 rather than farther away. Not by a whole lot, Redmond isn't very big and Microsoft is on the Bellevue side of it. Also, there are now Microsoft buildings in Bellevue and Seattle as well, not sure when they put them in though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:48:00-07:00","id":989582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=989579#post989579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, no problem. Just pointing out that Microsoft was actually closer to Seattle proper between 79 and 86 rather than farther away. Not by a whole lot, Redmond isn't very big and Microsoft is on the Bellevue side of it. Also, there are now Microsoft buildings in Bellevue and Seattle as well, not sure when they put them in though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is good to know, at least.<br /> <br /> I do have a question - what's up with this Seattle Freeze thing in Splintered Seattle? I tried googling but got some questions with uninformative answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:55:11-07:00","id":989585,"title":"","content":"Basically, its a name (not something that is actually used much around here but I've heard it from outsiders) for the passive, faux-polite brush off busy people in Seattle tend to do. It's similar to other west coast platitudes about meeting someone later. Essentially, let's say you see a person you know when you are grabbing your morning latte and you have a short exchange of pleasantries and then they say that 'you two should catch-up sometime, have coffee or a drink' but then you will never hear from them. I have also heard it explained that it is not really intended to be rude, its just that Seattlites tend to be very busy and work obsessed people, so they never get around to calling you up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:53:57-07:00","id":989616,"title":"","content":"what's interesting to me is that neighborhoods that appeal to influential mortals might not be prime havens for vampires. I think elders would be looking for that sweet spot between herd density and political influence.<br /> <br /> A poor neighborhood that houses the city's historically black colleges might not be an appealing place for well-to-do-mortals to buy a home, but the high population density, lack of police patrols, and access to the brightest up-and-coming intellectuals would make it fallow ground for an elder to roost in. Similarly, an area that houses a lot of workers who labor for the city's largest industry might be poor and rundown but also gives an enterprising vampire the potential to greatly influence the local labor unions.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin, you have a rich suburb that hosts some well-to-do mortals but is also far from the political levers of the city, more tightly patrolled, and more sparsely populated. This might be the kind of territory that princes and council members rent out to trusted vassals. I think younger vampires are more likely to jump at the possibility of living somewhere with mortal prestige whereas elders are more likely to take a pragmatic approach to where they establish themselves.<br /> <br /> Then there's the vast stretches of blighted territory that are of little use to anyone which are probably filled with kindred squatters, coteries, and outlaws. Still, these places have their own value for creative kindred. A cardinal of the Lancaea Sanctum, a recruiter for the Circle of the Crone, or an anarchist firestarter in the Carthians could make great use of the populations here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-18-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:45:06-07:00","id":990642,"title":"","content":"So in my Carthians-over-threw-the-Invictus in Portland Oregon<br /> <br /> (I am actually running a Longview Washington Game &lt;in that the game begins as an <i><b>Innocents</b></i> game in Longview Washington&gt; but am populating the surrounding world so it isn't something I need to do on the fly when the PCs leave their little isolated area)<br /> <br /> It works like this:<br /> <br /> Within the Portland Protectorate (not to be confused for or affiliated with the werewolf term) are three branches of Government, Executive, Legislative and Judicial. Keeping with the principle of separation of power, each Kindred may only hold One Office at a time and forfeits a previously held Office by accepting a new one.<br /> <br /> The Judicial the strongest Branch as they arbitrate conflicts between vampires, and make rulings on the guilt of vampires who transgress against the law. There are three Reeves who are always Carthians which is the entirety of the Judicial Branch and is very much a triumvirate. They also set the standards for the Competitions by which Councilors of Domains are chosen, and collectively count ballets in all elections. When society is ruled by laws, as Carthian society is, it is the judges that wield final authority. They hold the positions are as long as they are able to carry out the duties of the office, and should one be torpored or meet Final Death, the remaining Reeve(s) would select the most appropriate Carthian replacement(s) from the Legislative Branch. This has never happened, nor has the entire Judicial Branch been wiped out, but if it was one of two things would happen, if the Carthians had enough strength to continue to enforce the rule of law then the Council of Domains nominates candidates by vote of hands, which would be confirmed by the Council of Covenants by vote of hands, or if the Carthians lacked the strength/support then the entire system would collapse.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is a Sheriff who is the head of the Executive Branch and acts to investigate/punish for the Judicial Branch, and is elected by popular semi-open vote (Only the three Reeves see the Ballets) of the entire Portland Metro Area (minus Vancouver Washington) every score of years, subject to the Veto of the Judicial Branch, which must be Unanimous among the three to enact their right of Veto, and is usually done based on the Sheriff not being suitable to the tasks needed or actively hostile against the Carthian Movement. The Sheriff may have a single deputy from each official neighborhood within Portland and also one from each suburb town also controlled by the Portland Protectorate. The Sheriff is subject to punishments enacted by the Reeves both for overstepping authority and failing in her duties, and in kind has that authority over her deputies. The Sheriff and her deputies have the authority to apprehend anyone violating the law and bring them before the Judicial for judgment, and execute those found guilty of capital offenses, and ensure the penalties are carried out for lesser offenses.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Legislative branch is the masterpiece of the entire system, it gives amazing power distributed and diluted to many petty tyrants and makes them jockey to maintain power, which keeps them invested in the current power scheme, while also keeping up-and-comers hopeful for their shot. The Legislative Branch is divided into two Councils, the Council of Domain and the Council of Covenants. Member of Councils go by the title Councilor, and the two different Councils bestow radically different powers upon their members.<br /> <br /> Each Councilor of the Council of Domains holds power over and is responsible for a single official neighborhood of Portland or one of the suburb towns also controlled by the Portland Protectorate. They alone hold the right to grant feeding privileges or safe haven within the section of the Protectorate they oversee, with squatting or poaching being serious offenses which is punishable with increasing severity based on the number and gravity of offenses, according to the guidelines in the Law and discretion of the Reeves. Specifically the guidelines for types of offenses hold the Councilor in charge of the neighborhood or suburb town the beneficiary to with fines are paid and \u201ccommunity service\u201d is levied for. Frequently a Councilor of the Council of Domains with curry favor with the Deputy of their area, the Sheriff, the Reeves, other Councilors, and various powerful individuals with prime selection of Safe Haven and Feeding Grounds, which are defined via the Official Plat Map for both clarity and ambiguity.<br /> <br /> The Councilor of the Council of Domains is responsible the beneficial for Kindred condition of their neighborhood or suburb town, and the city\u2019s Kindred population in general. This applies to non-Kindred facets of the Protectorate, like the local mortal economy, homeless populations, club scenes, apparent lack of violent crime, and ease of maintaining the masquerade. Kindred are governed by the Law, and thus an appropriate Deputy and the Sheriff handle those matters. It is true that a Councilor from the Council of Domains almost always accomplishes their responsibilities by deals and alliances with other Kindred, but it is their head on the chopping block if they fail. Councilors of the Council of Domains Register all Feeding Grounds and Safe Havens they bestow with the Reeves and the appropriate Councilor from the Council of Covenants. In addition to controlling Feeding Grounds and Safe Havens, all Laws of the Protectorate originate in the Council of Domains, and must meet a four-fifths majority before being passed to the Council of Covenants.<br /> <br /> The members of the Council of Domains earn their position competing in a contest set by the Reeves to demonstrate capacity to steward and manage the area, and must re-compete as which domain is hosting the contest cycles, in a set order adding newly annexed suburbs next in the roster. Contest have ranged from demonstrating the most control over some mortal institution(s) that is relevant to managing the area, being the first to quell a particular problem for Kindred in the area. The first method favors the incumbent and the second put him on much more equal footing with his contenders, and thus it behooves the incumbent to leave no problems that can be turned into contest by the Reeves, and to maintain a firm grip on the human institutions that are the heart of his domain. The genius of the system is three fold, first the since there is one Domain in contest annually it keeps a constant opportunity for ambitious Kindred to claim their piece of the pie and ambitious kindred without opportunities are dangerous, secondly it keeps individual domain and the protectorate at large relatively stable because only a small sector may change in power structure, and it thirdly makes this Council a very diverse group of kindred as originators of the laws which means it is likely they\u2019ll only be able to gather the needed consensus on absolute commonly essential laws.<br /> <br /> The Council of Covenants has only five Councilors, one for each Covenant and who is voted in by preferential open ballet vote of the members of their Covenant, with every member of that Covenant with Havens or Feeding Grounds inside a Domain within the Portland Protectorate being listed as Candidates. Candidates may only withdrawal from the race by forfeit/abandoning their qualifying Haven/Feeding Grounds, entering Torpor, or by already holding another Office within the Protectorate. Each member of each Covenant who has qualifying Safe Havens or Feeding Grounds within the Portland Protectorate personally hands their ballet into the Reeves who keep them on record for those interested in knowing how each member voted. Votes occur on a rotating cycle on every four years starting in 1956 (Last four elections: 2000 Lance Sanctum, 2004 Circle of the Crone, 2008 Ordo Dracul, 2012 Carthian, 2016 Invictus, ect...). The primary power of the Councilors of the Council of Covenants is the ability to levy a minor favor called for the benefit of the Protectorate from each of the members of its Covenant that wasn\u2019t disqualified as a candidate when they won Office. Frequently Councilors of the Council of Domains, Deputies, or even the Sheriff petition Councilors of the Council of Covenants to use this power to help them fulfill their duties.<br /> <br /> Being assured voted in next term usually is a factor of balancing commanding respect for their authority over their Covenant and keeping a light touch at calling in the levy, and especially call in individual favors in a way that those doing the favor benefit from and enjoy the task. This cycle is about to complete for the third time this year. The Carthian Councilor position has never changed, which makes sense since the first elected Carthian was exceptionally politically savvy and the system was designed with their understanding of rule of law in mind The first elected Invictus Councilor was the former Gangrel Prince and was huge ineffective due to his direct violent temper/callously autocratic leadership and voted out after her first term. The current Invictus Councilor is far more Machiavellian and seems to be sealing a second term this year. The Lance Sanctum and Circle of the Crone have had major upsets during their last two elections after their initial incumbents won their first re-election, both of which reflect changes in their potential herds/blood cults. The Ordo Dracul seems elect their weakest and least experienced member each election cycle, who is then bullied into not asking too much in levies, with a rumor among other covenants that the last two cycles the Ordo Dracul Councilor was specifically newly embraced a week before the election to fulfill that role. Interestingly, the Ordo Dracul Councilor seems to mature quickly under the pressures, and thus always overqualified for a second term.<br /> <br /> The second power that Councilors of the Council or Covenants is that all potential laws received from the Council of Domains must have a four-fifths majority to enacted as law. Third and finally every law on record is to be voted upon on the twentieth anniversary of being enacted into law and again have a four-fifths majority to remain in law (This does not apply to the original Protectorate Charter, but does apply to amendments).<br /> <br /> Running about roughly 100 Vampire population to justify the complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-21-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:54:01-07:00","id":990648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=990642#post990642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in my Carthians-over-threw-the-Invictus in Portland Oregon</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what I read but your two really really long paragraphs are difficult for me to get through. Could you add more paragraph breaks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T21:59:56-07:00","id":990793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985695-carthian-ruled-domain?p=990642#post990642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in my Carthians-over-threw-the-Invictus in Portland Oregon<br /> <br /> (I am actually running a Longview Washington Game &lt;in that the game begins as an <i><b>Innocents</b></i> game in Longview Washington&gt; but am populating the surrounding world so it isn't something I need to do on the fly when the PCs leave their little isolated area)<br /> <br /> <br /> Running about roughly 100 Vampire population to justify the complexity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the paragraph breaks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for the fully detailed rundown on how Portland works in your game. This gives me a lot to think about and more ideas to reach for. I especially like the details on how the kindred in the domain vote for offices. It is also making me rethink how I want to handle the council in Seattle. Also to put a lot more thought into neighborhoods.<br /> <br /> I wish I had more of a response to do justice to your post but I'm still processing it.<br /> <br /> I was originally going to run my game in Portland, but one of the players-to-be pushed for Seattle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}